---
import SimplePage from '../../components/SimplePage.astro';
import { routes, routeUrl } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { profile } from '../../data/profile';
---

<SimplePage lang="en" alternates={routes.privacy} title="Privacy policy">
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">
    Last updated: November 2026. This is an English translation for convenience; the legally binding version is the
    <a href={routeUrl('privacy', 'de')} lang="de">German Datenschutzerklärung</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Controller</h2>
  <address>
    {profile.name}<br />
    {profile.address.street}<br />
    {profile.address.zipCity}, Germany<br />
    Email: <a href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>{profile.email}</a>
  </address>

  <h2>2. Overview</h2>
  <p>
    This is a personal portfolio website. It uses <strong>no cookies</strong>, <strong>no tracking</strong> and
    <strong>no analytics tools</strong>. Fonts are served directly from this website, so no connection is made to
    Google Fonts or other font providers. Personal data is only processed where technically necessary to operate the
    website or when you voluntarily send me a message.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Hosting (Cloudflare)</h2>
  <p>
    This website is delivered via Cloudflare, provided by Cloudflare, Inc., 101 Townsend St., San Francisco,
    CA 94107, USA. When you visit the website, Cloudflare automatically processes information transmitted by your
    browser, in particular your IP address, date and time of access, the page requested, the referrer and
    browser/operating system information. This is necessary to deliver the website securely and reliably and to
    protect it against attacks.
  </p>
  <p>
    The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR; my legitimate interest is the reliable and secure provision of this website.
    Data may be transferred to the USA. Cloudflare is certified under the EU-US Data Privacy Framework. See the
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>
    for details.
  </p>
  <h3>Audience measurement (Cloudflare Web Analytics)</h3>
  <p>
    I use Cloudflare Web Analytics to evaluate page views statistically. It sets no cookies, uses no fingerprinting
    and creates no profiles of individual visitors. Only aggregated data such as pages visited, referrer, country,
    device type and load times is collected. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR; my legitimate interest is
    understanding how the website is used.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Contact form (Web3Forms)</h2>
  <p>
    If you use the contact form, the details you enter (name, email address, optionally your company, and your message)
    are sent to the service <strong>Web3Forms</strong>, which forwards the message to me by email. Processing may take place outside the EU,
    in particular in the USA. See the
    <a href="https://web3forms.com/privacy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Web3Forms privacy policy</a> for details.
  </p>
  <p>
    The purpose is to process and answer your enquiry. The legal basis is Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR where your enquiry relates
    to a potential employment or contractual relationship, otherwise Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in
    answering enquiries), as well as your consent under Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR given via the checkbox in the form. You can
    withdraw your consent at any time with effect for the future, e.g. by email.
  </p>
  <p>
    I delete your message once it has been fully dealt with, unless statutory retention obligations apply. In the
    context of a recruitment process, the usual retention periods apply.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Contact by email</h2>
  <p>
    If you email me, I process your details solely to deal with your enquiry, based on Art. 6(1)(b) or (f) GDPR. The
    data is deleted once it is no longer needed for this purpose.
  </p>

  <h2>6. External links</h2>
  <p>
    This website contains links, e.g. to LinkedIn. Data is only transferred to the respective provider once you click
    such a link; that provider is responsible for any processing there.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you have the right to</p>
  <ul>
    <li>access your personal data (Art. 15),</li>
    <li>rectification (Art. 16),</li>
    <li>erasure (Art. 17),</li>
    <li>restriction of processing (Art. 18),</li>
    <li>data portability (Art. 20),</li>
    <li>object to processing based on Art. 6(1)(f) (Art. 21), and</li>
    <li>withdraw consent at any time with effect for the future (Art. 7(3)).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You also have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority (Art. 77 GDPR), e.g. the
    State Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of Information of Baden-Württemberg.
  </p>
  <p>An informal email to the address above is sufficient for any request.</p>
</SimplePage>
